      "title": "Georgia's additional declared holiday on the official 2026 state schedule\n(O.C.G.A. § 1-4-1(a)(2)): Good Friday, April 3; November 27; and\nDecember 24 (the observed Washington’s Birthday). The statute makes days\nproclaimed by the Governor public and legal holidays; annual dates are not\nprojected without a published schedule. The federal holidays enumerated\nby § 1-4-1(a)(1) are already in `us-federal-holidays`."
